        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "30a979ab-0717-561c-a62f-34f59b38fd3b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Gaillardia, Browningia, Helenium\n- Taxonomy: Asteraceae, Helenieae, Helianthodae, Anthroismeae, Coreopsideae, Eupatorieae, Heliantheae, Inuleae, Tageteae\n\nFacts:\n- Gaillardia, commonly called blanket flower, is a genus of flowering plants in the family Asteraceae and is native to North and South America.\n- Browningia is a genus of cacti with 11 accepted species and 3 unresolved species.\n- In the tribe Helenieae, Helenium is the type genus, and Gaillardia is among the best known members.\n- Helianthodae is a supertribe in the family Asteraceae that contains the tribes Anthroismeae, Coreopsideae, Eupatorieae, Helenieae, Heliantheae, Inuleae, and Tageteae.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
